          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
            %em properness
            is that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compactness
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            between them.
          %p
            A continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            is proper when “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is compact, relative to
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p There are three inequivalent definitions of a proper map in the literature, of strictly increasing strength.
          %p The first one is the oldest definition, still found in some analysis books.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is
              %strong proper
              if it is
              %strong quasi-proper
              (alias
              = succeed "):" do
                %strong lax proper
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
              subset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K\subset Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}K
              is a compact subset of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The second definition was introduced by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bourbaki"} Bourbaki
            to make proper maps closed under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+changes"} base changes
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is
              %strong proper
              if it is
              = succeed ":" do
                %strong universally closed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              of topological spaces.
          %p Other equivalent characterizations include the following:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                the map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi Z
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\times id_Z\colon X\times Z\to Y\times Z
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
            %li
              %p
                The map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is quasi-proper and closed.
            %li
              %p
                The map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is closed and every fiber of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
          %p
            The third definition was introduced by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+spaces"} compact Hausdorff spaces
            are to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+spaces"} compact spaces
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              is
              %strong proper
              if it is universally closed and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+map"} separated
          %p
            Recall that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+map"} separated
            if its relative diagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X\times_Y X
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y=\{*\}
            is the terminal
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            compact and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff"} Hausdorff
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
            is automatically separated, which makes the last two definitions equivalent.
          %p
            The following criterion explains the necessary and sufficient criterion on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            that ensures that quasi-proper maps to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are universally closed.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              (Whyburn 1965, Palais 1969.) The following properties of a topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              are equivalent:
            %ul
              %li
                Every quasi-proper map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %li
                Every surjective quasi-proper map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %li
                Every injective quasi-proper map
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to Y
                is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %li
                Every compactly closed subset of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                is closed.
            %p
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is Hausdorff, the last condition is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            being a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+space"} compactly generated space
          %h2#equivalent_definitions_of_universally_closed_maps Equivalent definitions of universally closed maps
          %p
            Just like there are various equivalent ways of characterizing
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
          %p In the following we discuss:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#UsingNets"}> characterization via nets
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#UsingClosedSets"}> characterization via intersection of closed sets
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#UsingClosedness"}> characterization via closedness
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#AsAContinousFamilyOfCompactSpaces"}> characterization as a continuous family of compact fibres
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#FurtherCharacterizations"}> further characterizations
                \.
          %h3#UsingNets Via nets
          %p
            Recall that for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            means for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
            in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+of+a+net"} convergent
            subnet.
          %p
            A generalisation of this characterisation to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            is the following:
          %p
          #PropernessViaNets.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \,\colon\, X \to Y
              is
              %em universally closed
              if and only if for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_\bullet)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
              has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
            %p Equivalently:
            %p
              Such
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is universally closed if and only if for every net
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet \in X
              and every
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_\bullet)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+of+a+net"} converges
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
              admits a subnet
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convergence+of+a+net"} converging
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
            %p
          %h3#UsingClosedSets Via intersection of closed sets
          %p
            Recall that, equivalently, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            if and only if for every cofiltered set of non-empty closed subsets
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_i \subset X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cap_i F_i
            is also non-empty.
          %p
          #PropernessViaClosedSets.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is
              %em universally closed
              if and only if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is closed;
              %li
                %p
                  for every cofiltered set of closed subsets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{F_i\}_{i \in I}
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mo ∩
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\cap_{i \in I} F_i) = \cap_{i \in I}f(F_i)
            %p
          %h3#UsingClosedness Via closedness
          %p
            Recall that, equivalently, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            if and only if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection+map"} projection map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Z \longrightarrow Z
          %p
            out of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
            with some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
          %p
          #PropernessViaClosedness.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is
              %em universally closed
              if and only if its image under the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                      %mi Z
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \times \mathrm{Id}_Z \colon X \times Z \longrightarrow Y \times Z
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              for every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
          %h3#AsAContinousFamilyOfCompactSpaces As a continuous family of compact spaces
          %p
            With every function
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            can be described as the union of the fibres
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(y)
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is proper when each fibre is compact and the family is continuous in the sense that: for every net
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_\bullet
            converging to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(y_\bullet)
            converges to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(y)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            be closed.
          %p
          #PropernessAsAContinuousFamilyOfCompactFibres.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is
              %em universally closed
              if:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(\{y\})
                  is compact for every
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is closed.
            %p
          %h3#FurtherCharacterizations Further characterizations
          %p
          #EquivalenceOfCharacterization.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropernessViaNets"}
                %p
                  For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/net"} net
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  and every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi x
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_\bullet)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
                  admits a cluster point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                  with
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℱ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filter"} filter
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  and if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cluster+point"} cluster point
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℱ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\mathcal{F})
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℱ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
                  has a cluster point
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                  with
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) = y
              %li
                %p
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropernessViaClosedSets"}
                %p
                  The map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
                  and for every cofiltered family
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{F_i\}_{i \in I}
                  of closed subsets of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mo ∩
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mo ∩
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\cap_{i \in I} F_i) = \cap_{i \in I}f(F_i)
              %li
                %p
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropernessViaClosedness"}
                %p
                  The image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                          %mi Z
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \times \mathrm{Id}_Z \,\colon\, X \times Z \to Y \times Z
                  under the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
                  for every topological space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Z
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universally+closed+morphism"}> universally closed
                  )
                %p
                  For every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi Z
                          %mo →
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon Z \to Y
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                  map
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^\ast(f)\colon X \times_Y Z \to Z
                %p
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              %li
                %p
                  (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropernessAsAContinuousFamilyOfCompactFibres"}
                %p
                  The map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}\big(\{y\}\big)
                  of every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \in Y
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %li
                %p
                  The map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
                  and the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+image"} inverse image
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(K)
                  of every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subspace"} compact subspace
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset Y
                  is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            %p
          %p
            (cf.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Bourbaki71"} Bourbaki 1971
          %p
          #ProperContinuous.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps"}> proper maps
                )
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f  \colon X \to Y
              is called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+map"} universally closed
              if it satisfies one of the equivalent properties listed in Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalenceOfCharacterization"}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Ambiguous terminology)
              %br/
              The notion of compact space is subject to naming ambiguity. For the same notion, some authors will use the term
              = succeed "," do
                %em quasi-compact
              %em compact
              only when the space is also separated.
            %p
              For
              %em properness
              the situation is
              %em worse
              as there are three competing definitions. We have defined the one similar to
              %em quasi-compact
              spaces.
            %p
              In addition one could require
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              to be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+map"} separated
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_\bullet
              converges to both
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_1) = f(x_2)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 = x_2
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+morphism"} proper morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+base+change+theorem"} proper base change theorem
            %p
              Finally, some authors use a weaker version of properness (defined above as quasi-properness), where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              is quasi-proper when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(K)
              is compact for every compact
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset Y
          %h2#further_criteria Further criteria
          %p
            A quasi-proper map, i.e., a continuous map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(K)
            is compact for every compact
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset Y
            may not be closed; even when both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are very nice spaces like
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi T
                    %mn 5
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}_5
            spaces.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be an uncountable set and let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for the discrete topological space associated to it. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_p
              denote the topological space whose underlying set is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              but whose opens sets are either all the sets not containing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              or the sets containing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              with countable complement in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_p
              is a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi T
                      %mn 5
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{T}_5
              topological space and its compact subsets are all finite. But the identity map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \longrightarrow X_p
            %p is not closed.
          %p
            However this is very often the case in practice: for example when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a metric space or a locally compact separated space.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
              be a continuous map such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(K)
                  is compact for every compact
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo ⊂
                          %mi Y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset Y
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+space"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                    \-space
            %p
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is closed and thus universally closed.
          %p Also,
          #MapsFromCompactSpacesToHausdorffSpacesAreClosed.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (maps from compact spaces to separated spaces are proper)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Y
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+topological+space"} separated
            %p
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is universally closed.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            Proper maps enjoy analogous properties as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+spaces"} compact topological spaces
            do, for example the product of proper maps (with or without the separation condition) is again proper:
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{f_i \colon X_i \to Y_i\}_{i \in I}
              be a small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indexed+family"} indexed family
              of universally closed maps (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProperContinuous"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i \in I} f_i \colon \prod_{i \in I} X_i \longrightarrow \prod_{i \in I} Y_i
            %p
              is also a universally closed map. If the maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
              are
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated+maps"} separated maps
          %p Further properties:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+maps+to+locally+compact+spaces+are+closed"} proper maps to locally compact spaces are closed
          %h2#comparison_with_proper_maps_of_locales Comparison with proper maps of locales
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X\to Y
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
              is
              %strong universally closed
              if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
              %strong separated
              if the relative diagonal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\to X\times_Y X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
              of locales, and
              %strong proper
              if it is universally closed and separated.
          %p
            These three notions can also be defined categorically by considering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            as an object in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Loc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Loc/Y
            and recalling that the latter category is equvialent to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of sheaves of sets on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            satisfies these properties if the corresponding internal locale is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated"} separated
            (meaning the diagonal map is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locales"} locales
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact"} compact
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separated"} separated
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every proper map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon X \to Y
              between two topological spaces induces a proper map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Loc}(f)\colon \mathrm{Loc}(X) \to \mathrm{Loc}(Y)
              between the associated locales.
            %p
              Conversely, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Loc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Loc}(f)\colon \mathrm{Loc}(X) \to \mathrm{Loc}(Y)
              is proper and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is a
              = succeed "-space," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} T
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{T}_\mathrm{D}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\,:\, X \to Y
              is proper.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+proper+map"} locally proper map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+morphism"} proper morphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"}> open map
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+map"} closed map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+group+action"} proper group action
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+homotopy"} proper homotopy
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} proper equivariant homotopy theory
          %h2#references References
          %p All three definitions are presented in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stacks+Project"}> Stacks Project
              , Tag 005M,
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/005M"} https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/005M
          %p Equivalence of the first and second definition is explored in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+S.+Palais"}> Richard S. Palais
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em When proper maps are closed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/s0002-9939-1970-0254818-x"} doi
          %p One of the early reference on proper maps is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              %em Topologie Générale
              (Éléments de Mathématique, Livre III), Chapitres 1 à 2. Second Edition, 1951. Actualites Sci. Ind. 1142, Hermann, Paris.
          %p An expanded treatment is given in the third edition, see Chapter I, Section 10:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              %em Topologie Générale
              (Éléments de Mathématique, Livre III), Chapitres 1 à 2. Third Edition, 1961. Actualites Sci. Ind. 1142, Hermann, Paris.
          %p English translation of the 1971 edition:
          %ul
            %li#Bourbaki71
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"}> Nicolas Bourbaki
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em General topology
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61701-0"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61701-0
          %p#LocaliVersionReferences
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} localic
            version of proper maps was introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              , §1 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Gleason cover of a topos, II
              %strong 22
              3 (1981) 229–247 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(81)90100-6"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(81)90100-6
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p where it is attributed to this “preliminary” (and apparently unpublished) account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Factorization and pullback theorems for localic geometric morphisms
          %p Additional sources:
          %ul
            %li
              J. J. C. Vermeulen,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Proper maps of locales
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(94)90047-7"} doi
          %ul
            %li
              M. Korostenski, C. C. A. Labuschagne,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lax proper maps of locales
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2006.03.003"} doi
        .revisedby
